title The refusal that named its cost and never its cause
prompt autonomous lap -- fleet baton, incense lane: law, active-designing, iterative review
rota lap 4682, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; hand-advanced past row 2, which pheromone read today. The threshold asks a lap to listen for the silence where a claim used to be and a witness now stands. It heard one: the runner says a pass was thrown away and says nothing about why.
think Opened with fleet_round_open, then launched the cold roster pass detached per the baton's own naming rule.
think Read the aether triad -- the compass, the Lindy effect, the grain -- and the grain's own strand: a guard that cannot red guards nothing.
think Chose control-legs as the crux at first: 234 paired control+witness families, 32 controls print a leg count, 27 read by their witness. Claimed it.
think The claim wrote construction/fleet-claims.kyri, the cold pass closed tree_moved=yes, and 272 green guards over 3232 guard-seconds were rightly thrown away.
think The transcript named the cost and never the cause -- and the cause was the baton's own instruction to claim before building. Copal reported the same shape one lap earlier. A lantern fired twice, so it is a loom.
think Withdrew the control-legs claim, opened tree-moved-names, pushed it, then built.
think tree_paths() emits one hash-and-path line per path differing from HEAD or untracked, plus HEAD's own, written to the runner's mktemp pen at open and at close. One awk at the close prints three verbs, bounded at sixteen with the remainder counted.
obs The pen caught the verb. A first draft read verbs off set membership, so a committed file rewritten mid-pass read appeared -- it stands in no open listing at all, because it was clean when the pass opened. The listing holds what differs from HEAD, never the tree. Each verb is now asserted apart; one leg standing for three would have passed on whichever happened to work.
obs Two mutations bite: collapsing changed into appeared reds named_changed, and lifting the bound reds named_bound_rows=16.
obs Three own-goals, all the same class and all undone: a no-op git commit -F .lap/commit-msg.txt committed a previous lap's body; the shelf tool shelved a previous lap's block from a stale .lap/incense-block.txt; and a git stash pop typed in the shared tree aborted rather than applying a peer's stash. read-scope names the .lap/ hazard in prose and no guard reaches it.
obs The pin is deadlocked -- 17 rows, 0 foldable, 0 fit -- so both reds are keyed by stamp rather than numbered.
loom witness=standing_equipment control_legs_added=9 mutations_bitten=2
loom tool=tree_paths wall_ms=162 dirty_paths=3 calls_per_pass=2
loom pass=standing_equipment_cold guards_green=272 guards_red=0 guards_seconds=3232 verdict=tree_moved
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_run.sh tree_paths beside tree_digest, and the three-verb naming at the close
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_control.sh nine legs proving each verb apart plus the bound from both sides
file tools/s/standing_equipment_witness.rish the nine legs asserted by name, so the pen is heard
file active-designing/20260912-050057_the-refusal-that-named-its-cost.md the paper, B+ 87, checkable room
file construction/ITINERARY.md the INCENSE account, elder shelved, one question for Keaton
file construction/archive/20260912-050057_itinerary-landed-accounts.md the elder account, links re-anchored by the writer
